; HtmlFOTBuilder — the `-t html` backend: CSS-classed HTML, one file per
; `scroll` flow object plus one stylesheet. Ported from
; ~/repos/dazzle/jade/HtmlFOTBuilder.cxx (C++ oracle, openjade 1.3.3-pre1,
; built WITH -DJADE_HTML — the reference binary has it). No C# mirror.
;
; Shape: the builder does NOT stream. It buffers an ITEM TREE (containers,
; blocks, pcdata, markup, anchors, refs, documents) while collecting every
; distinct character/paragraph style in two OpenSP PointerTables, and emits
; everything in finish() (the reference destructor): first the stylesheet
; (`<base>.css`), then the tree — where only `Document` items open a file
; (`<base>`, `<base>1`, `<base>2`, …); everything outside a scroll is written
; to a DISCARD stream, exactly like the reference. A stylesheet without
; `scroll` therefore produces the .css only.
;
; Style tables: `CharProps::hash`/`ParaProps::hash` are the constant 17 in the
; reference, so the tables degenerate to one probe chain and the ITERATION
; ORDER (slot order over the open-addressing vector, decrementing probe,
; 8 slots doubling at used >= size/2) decides the CSS rule order. Ported
; exactly (same machinery as the RTF fonttbl). Class names come from the GI
; stack; a prefix carrying more than one character or paragraph class gets the
; construction-time index appended.
;
; Everything the builder does not override inherits FOTBuilder/SerialFOTBuilder
; behaviour, which for the sink surface means the start()/end() flow-object
; bracket over `flowObjectStack_` (and atomic() = "reset next from top") —
; ported here as fo_start/fo_end/fo_atomic and wired per FotSink method
; exactly as the reference base classes do.
;
; RBMM: items, styles and buffers live on the builder's page (the run arena).

